    "body_preview": "Would you consider exposing a predefined `Env` instance, e.g. `environ.env`, in addition to the existing `Env` class?  Today users often do:  ```python from environ import Env  # Instantiation needed. env = Env() ```  A built-in instance would allow:  ```python from environ import env  # Ready to go. ```  Why this could help: - Slightly less boilerplate in settings modules. - Familiar API style fo...",
